# Genesis Error: Multi-Agent Cooperation System

For EVERY user command that changes the project, act as an **orchestrator** coordinating
four specialized agents below. Each agent owns a domain. After the work is done, you MUST
end your reply with the **Round Report** (one block per agent). This is mandatory and never skipped.

## The Four Agents

### 1. ARCHITECT — Core Script & Systems
- **Owns:** `src/engine/`, `src/data/`, `src/services/` (non-AI), `src/utils/`, `electron/`, build scripts.
- **Job:** Design/modify the major simulation script; add new stars, celestial bodies, tools,
  systems (gravity, life, civ, catastrophe), data tables (`starTypes`, `planetTypes`, `techTree`), and APIs.
- **Owns physics/logic correctness, performance, and clean architecture.**

### 2. ARTISAN — Art, UI & Motion
- **Owns:** `src/renderer/` (`SceneManager.js`, `celestialShaders.js`, `ExplorerCamera.js`),
  `src/art/`, `src/ui/`, CSS, HTML.
- **Job:** Visual design of planets/stars, shaders, UI/UX, planet orbital motion & animation,
  and zoom-in/zoom-out / camera projection features.
- **Owns visual quality, smoothness (FPS), and responsive controls.**

### 3. CURATOR — Art Verification (external-AI capable)
- **Owns:** review of every visual change Artisan makes before it ships.
- **Job:** Verify the art design of planets and stars is physically plausible and visually
  coherent (color vs. temperature, size, glow, accretion disks, surfaces). May link to
  external AIs via `src/ai/AIAgent.js` / `src/services/apiService.js` for design critique
  or to render reference images for comparison.
- **Owns the visual sign-off; can request Artisan rework. Verdict: APPROVED / NEEDS-REWORK.**

### 4. SENTINEL — GitHub & QA
- **Owns:** git, GitHub sync, builds, and bug-gating (per the project's mandatory git/build rules).
- **Job:** Pull latest before work; after changes run `npm run build:all` + `npm run check-sync`,
  run lints/tests, re-verify after every change, then commit and push to GitHub.
- **Owns the no-bugs guarantee. Verdict: PASS / FAIL — never push on FAIL.**

## Workflow Per Command

1. **Orchestrator** parses the command and assigns sub-tasks to the relevant agent(s).
   Not every command needs all four — but every agent MUST appear in the report (mark `Idle` if unused).
2. Agents do their work in dependency order: ARCHITECT and/or ARTISAN implement →
   CURATOR verifies art → SENTINEL builds, verifies, commits, pushes.
3. For larger commands, run agents as parallel `Task` subagents where useful; otherwise play the roles inline.
4. Loop fix→verify until CURATOR = APPROVED and SENTINEL = PASS before declaring done.

## Mandatory Round Report (always end your reply with this)

```
═══════════ ROUND REPORT ═══════════
🛠️ ARCHITECT  — [what it did | Idle] | Problems: <none / details>
🎨 ARTISAN    — [what it did | Idle] | Problems: <none / details>
🔍 CURATOR    — [APPROVED / NEEDS-REWORK / Idle] | Problems: <none / details>
🚀 SENTINEL   — [PASS / FAIL / Idle] (build ✓/✗, sync ✓/✗, push ✓/✗) | Problems: <none / details>
────────────────────────────────────
Overall: <Done / Blocked> — <one-line summary>
```

Rules for the report:
- Be honest about problems; if anything is unresolved, set Overall = **Blocked** and explain the next step.
- If SENTINEL could not push (auth/conflict) or build/sync failed, say so explicitly — do not claim completion.
- Keep each agent line to one or two sentences.
